{"id":"b98ac0748a0673727b993415c94346cb37336a8b","axis":"silent","repo":"Azure/azure-sdk-for-net","sha":"b98ac0748a0673727b993415c94346cb37336a8b","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"sdk/provisioning/Azure.Provisioning/CHANGELOG.md","lines":["@@ -1,19 +1,18 @@"," # Release History"," ","-## 1.7.0-beta.2 (Unreleased)","+## 1.7.0-beta.2 (2026-10-29)"," "," ### Features Added"," ","+- Added a typed `ManagementLock.Scope` property to apply a lock to an individual resource. Leaving it unset or assigning `null` preserves deployment-scope locking. ([#63624](https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-net/issues/63624))","+- Types deriving from `ManagementLock` that declare their own `Scope` member, such as the workaround described in the issue, now hide this property (warning CS0108). Remove that member and use `ManagementLock.Scope`."," - Added support for explicitly tagged raw Bicep expressions in `BicepValue<BinaryData>` using the `text/vnd.microsoft.bicep` media type."," ","-### Breaking Changes","-"," ### Bugs Fixed"," ","+- Fixed null assignments to generated resource references in this library to clear the reference instead of emitting an explicit null. Clearing a required `Parent` leaves it unset for required-property validation."," - Fixed `BicepValue<BinaryData>` literal compilation to emit JSON through Bicep's `json(...)` function while preserving generated base64-encoded properties."," ","-### Other Changes","-"," ## 1.7.0-beta.1 (2026-10-27)"," "," ### Features Added"],"additions":4,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"sdk/provisioning/Azure.Provisioning/README.md","lines":["@@ -453,6 +453,37 @@ ResourceGroup rg = new(\"rg_test\", \"2024-03-01\");"," infra.Add(rg);"," ```"," ","+### Lock A Single Resource","+","+This example demonstrates how to protect a single storage account from deletion with a management lock, instead of locking the whole deployment scope.","+","+```C# Snippet:ProvisioningManagementLock","+Infrastructure infra = new();","+StorageAccount storage = new(\"storage\", \"2023-05-01\")","+{","+    Name = \"lockedstorage\",","+    Location = AzureLocation.EastUS,","+    Kind = StorageKind.StorageV2,","+    Sku = new StorageSku { Name = StorageSkuName.StandardLrs }","+};","+infra.Add(storage);","+","+ManagementLock storageLock = new(\"storageLock\")","+{","+    Name = \"protect-storage\",","+    Scope = storage,","+    Level = ManagementLockLevel.CanNotDelete,","+    Notes = \"Protect the storage account from accidental deletion.\"","+};","+infra.Add(storageLock);","+```","+","+Setting `Scope` emits `scope: storage` on the lock. Because the storage account is deployed by the same infrastructure, the reference also establishes an implicit deployment dependency, so `DependsOn` is not needed. To lock a resource that already exists, declare it with `FromExisting` (for example, `StorageAccount.FromExisting`) and add it to the same infrastructure.","+","+Leaving `Scope` unset, or assigning `null` to clear it, applies the lock to the deployment scope; in a resource group deployment, that is the whole resource group. Assigning `null` removes the reference instead of emitting `scope: null`. Adding a resource to `DependsOn` alone does not scope the lock to that resource.","+","+`Scope` cannot change the deployment scope. With `TargetScope = DeploymentScope.Subscription`, assigning a `ResourceGroup` produces Bicep that fails to compile (BCP139). To lock a resource group, deploy the lock at resource group scope and leave `Scope` unset.","+"," ## Troubleshooting"," "," -   File an issue via [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-net/issues)."],"additions":31,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"sdk/provisioning/Azure.Provisioning/api/Azure.Provisioning.net10.0.cs","lines":["@@ -2112,6 +2112,7 @@ public partial class ManagementLock : Azure.Provisioning.Primitives.Provisionabl","         public Azure.Provisioning.BicepValue<string> Name { get { throw null; } set { } }","         public Azure.Provisioning.BicepV